<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#benzoin-resin">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benzoin resin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as benzoin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benzoin resin is an aromatic balsamic resin obtained from trees of the genus Styrax, used as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a>, in perfume and in medicine. It was one of the forest products of the Sumatran interior, along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camphor">camphor</a> and aromatic woods. These goods supplemented the commercial revenues of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya Empire</a>, which derived most of its wealth from controlling maritime trade.</p></div>
